About the Role
You'll be the main contact for customers from enquiry to delivery. You'll prepare quotations, process orders, coordinate shipments with our internal teams, and make sure customers are well looked after the sale. This suits a detail-oriented person who enjoys keeping things running smoothly and dealing with customers.
Key Responsibilities

• Handle pre-sales enquiries and prepare accurate quotations promptly;

• Follow up proactively on outstanding quotations and orders to help convert sales;

• Manage end-to-end order processing, including order entry, PO verification, and invoicing;

• Work with internal teams (e.g. logistics, warehouse) to track shipment schedules and ensure on-time delivery;

• Provide post-sales support by updating customers on shipment status, gathering feedback, and meeting specific customer requirements;

• Assist with customer complaints, product returns, and replacements.

Requirements

• Diploma or higher in Sales/Marketing, Customer Service, Admin, Logistics, Supply Chain, Engineering, or a related field;

• Experience in inside sales, sales support, or industrial customer service is an advantage;

• Detail-oriented, with a strong sense of responsibility for the full sales fulfilment cycle;

• Self-motivated and able to work independently, taking initiative to get things done;

• Good team player with high integrity and strong communication skills;

• Bilingual in English and Mandarin, to liaise with Mandarin-speaking customers and suppliers;

• Fresh graduates are welcome to apply. Training will be provided.

Job Summary
We are seeking Technical Delivery Manager who will be responsible for driving end-to-end technology delivery and enterprise transformation initiatives, ensuring alignment with business objectives, technology strategy, and enterprise architecture. The role oversees project execution, technical implementation, stakeholder engagement, risk management, and supplier coordination to ensure successful delivery within agreed timelines, budgets, and quality standards.
Mandatory Skill-set

• Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, IT, Computing, Engineering, or related discipline;

• Minimum 7 years of experience in IT Project/Program Management, Technical Delivery, or Business Transformation;

• Proven experience in end-to-end technology project delivery and business transformation;

• Strong knowledge of SDLC, Agile, and project delivery methodologies;

• Experience managing project plans, budgets, risks, issues, dependencies, and multiple concurrent projects;

• Understanding of enterprise IT architecture, infrastructure, system integration, and information security;

• Experience coordinating SIT, UAT, security testing, and production implementation;

• Hands-on experience with RFI, RFP, RFQ, supplier management, and contract negotiations;

• Proficiency in JIRA, Confluence, GitLab, and MS Project;

• Strong stakeholder management, communication, negotiation, and problem-solving skills.

Desired Skill-set

• Experience in Banking or Financial Services industry;

• End-to-end delivery experience in one or more of the following:

• Enterprise / Digital Transformation;AI solutions and business adoption;

• Cloud solutions and migration;IT Infrastructure and Network transformation;

• Endpoint / Workplace Technology;

• Active Directory and Identity & Access Management (IAM);

• Experience working with enterprise architecture, cybersecurity, and regulatory requirements.

Responsibilities

• Lead end-to-end technology and enterprise transformation projects from planning through implementation;

• Drive project execution, ensuring alignment between business requirements, technology solutions, and strategic objectives;

• Manage cross-functional teams, technical workstreams, project timelines, budgets, risks, issues, and dependencies;

• Engage senior stakeholders and C-suite executives to drive decisions and resolve escalations;

• Coordinate technical implementation, system integration, production cutover, and post-implementation support;

• Collaborate with Architects, Security, Business, and Technology teams to ensure solutions meet enterprise architecture and security standards;

• Oversee SIT, UAT, performance testing, penetration testing, and remediation activities;

• Manage supplier engagement, RFI/RFP/RFQ processes, vendor evaluation, negotiations, and contract finalization;

• Monitor project investments, financials, delivery progress, and business value realization;

• Ensure project governance, documentation, reporting, and delivery standards are maintained.

